---
source: crates/mori-checker/src/tests.rs
description: "Code:\n\nprofile \"moriarty-beta/1\";\nagreement Stable {\n  domain Preview = { id: \"preview\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"preview\" };\n  asset USD = { domain: Preview, id: \"usd\", scale: 2, representation: \"native\" };\n  account alice = { domain: Preview, id: \"alice\" };\n  instrument coin = { domain: Preview, id: \"coin\", asset: USD };\n  const mint = stablecoin.mint(instrument: coin, owner: alice, supply: 1 USD, backing: 1 USD);\n}\n"
---
mori::check::instrument_missing_field

  × `stablecoin.mint` needs the instrument `coin` to have a `backing` field.
   ╭─[test.mori:7:16]
 6 │   instrument coin = { domain: Preview, id: "coin", asset: USD };
 7 │   const mint = stablecoin.mint(instrument: coin, owner: alice, supply: 1 USD, backing: 1 USD);
   ·                ───────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────
   ·                                                       ╰── `coin` has no `backing`
 8 │ }
   ╰────
  help: Add `backing` to the instrument's declaration, naming an asset:

            backing: USD,
